## 4️⃣ Checklist for Future Development

| ✅ | Item | How to verify |
|----|------|---------------|
| **A01** | All read/write endpoints are behind an authentication/authorization check. | Unit tests assert `401` when no JWT is sent. |
| **A02** | TLS enforced (HTTPS) for all external traffic. | `curl -I https://your‑host/health` – no `http://` reachable. |
| **A03** | All user‑supplied data is validated/sanitized (e.g., `express-validator`, Joi). | Schema validation middleware returns `400` on bad payloads. |
| **A04** | Rate limiting applied to auth‑related routes (login, password reset). | Simulate > 100 requests per 15 min → `429 Too Many Requests`. |
| **A05** | Security headers present (`X‑Content‑Type‑Options`, `X‑Frame‑Options`, `Content‑Security‑Policy`, `Strict-Transport-Security`). | `curl -I https://…` and inspect headers. |
| **A06** | Dependencies up‑to‑date, no known CVEs. | CI step `npm audit` passes. |
| **A07** | Passwords hashed with bcrypt (or Argon2) before storage. | Code review of user‑creation flow. |
| **A08** | Integrity check for any external scripts/resources (Subresource Integrity). | CSP `script-src` only allows trusted origins. |
| **A09** | Centralised logging with correlation IDs + alerting on `5xx` spikes. | Logs are shipped to ELK/Datadog and alerts configured. |
| **A10** | Any outbound request (e.g., webhook) validates URLs against a whitelist. | Review code before adding external calls. |

