| File / Code | What it does | Where the secrets live |
|------------|--------------|-----------------------|
| `require('dotenv').config()` (first line of **app.js**) | Calls the **dotenv** package at start‑up. It reads a file named **`.env`** (or any file you point it at) in the project root and copies every `KEY=VALUE` line into `process.env`. | In the repository you have a **`.env.test`** file that contains a handful of synthetic “canary” credentials (DB URL, AWS keys, Anthropic API key, Stripe key, Logfire token, etc.). If the app is started with `dotenv` pointed at that file (e.g., `dotenv -e .env.test node app.js` or by renaming it to `.env`), all of those values become environment variables that any part of the code can read via `process.env.<KEY>`. |
